{
  "_comment": [
    "Web of Science subject categories per venue. Clarivate's own classification —",
    "not derived, not inferred. Read from Journal Citation Reports (2025 JCR year)",
    "through Yonsei's subscription, except where a note says otherwise.",
    "",
    "Multi-label by nature: JASIST carries two categories, DIGITAL HEALTH four.",
    "Any facet built on this has to let a paper appear under each of them.",
    "",
    "COMPLETE: all 46 venues looked up.",
    "",
    "Three kinds of entry:",
    "  categories non-empty  — a journal, every paper in it inherits these.",
    "  perPaper: true        — a conference or book series. Proceedings are",
    "                          classified per record, not per venue: ISSI 2017 is",
    "                          in CPCI-S with two categories while ISSI 2023 is not",
    "                          indexed at all. Look these up in",
    "                          data/wos-categories-by-paper.json. A paper in one of",
    "                          these venues with no entry there fails the check",
    "                          script rather than falling back silently.",
    "  fallback              — searched and genuinely absent from the Core",
    "                          Collection. The one field here that is not",
    "                          Clarivate's; it exists so those papers still answer",
    "                          to a filter instead of vanishing from it.",
    "",
    "researchAreas appears where a record carries a Research Area but no subject",
    "category — that happens outside the Core Collection, and is the one direction",
    "in which the two schemes differ in coverage rather than in granularity.",
    "",
    "A caution learned the hard way: absent from JCR does NOT mean unclassified.",
    "JCR covers journals only, because it exists to compute impact factors. ESCI",
    "titles and every conference proceeding are classified in the Core Collection",
    "but have no JCR entry. Information Research is the example — no JCR record,",
    "but its papers carry an SSCI category.",
    "",
    "issn is the ISSN JCR lists, which is sometimes the print ISSN where our",
    "publication data holds the electronic one (JMIR: 1439-4456 here vs",
    "1438-8871 in ours), so match on venue name, not on ISSN alone."
  ],
